        "details": {
            "description": "<p>The restless spirits of the prophet Eivess and his followers force intruders to relive their deaths at the fangs of Yig's avatar.</p>",
            "disable": "<p>@Check[society|dc:38] (master) or @Check[religion|dc:40] (master) to convince the spirits that their horror has been over for millennia, or @Check[occultism|dc:38] (master) or @Check[intimidation|dc:42] to recognize that this avatar exists only in the memories of the tormented spirits and command it to stand down; three total successes are required to disable the haunt</p>",
            "isComplex": true,
            "level": {
                "value": 20
            },
            "publication": {
                "license": "ORC",
                "remaster": true,
                "title": "Pathfinder Adventure Path #225: Vaultlines"
            },
            "reset": "",
            "routine": "<p>(3 actions) The avatar uses its first action each round to Devour Faithful, then attempts to Strike and swallow a frightened creature within 20 feet. If no nearby creatures are frightened, the avatar continues using its actions to Devour Faithful until a frightened victim becomes available.</p>"
        },
